(FIL-64: Write accepts a string literal, a buffer and the special value `a newline`, and the file handle's size property tracks the bytes written live.
 Also covers: FIL-65, FIL-66, FIL-67.
 13 + 1 + 3 + 1 = 18. size reads 0 before the first write and 18 after the
 last, so a generator that knows what it wrote can assert the size.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-64.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   0
   18
   18
   Hello, World!
   BUF
  
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
a buffer called payload is 16 bytes in size.
append "BUF" to payload.
open a file for writing called output at "vf_scratch/files/written.txt".
print output's size.
Write "Hello, World!" to output.
Write a newline to output.
Write payload to output.
Write a newline to output.
print output's size.
Close output.
open a file for reading called back at "vf_scratch/files/written.txt".
print back's size.
a buffer called contents is 64 bytes in size.
Read from back into contents.
print contents.
Close back.
